# Everything built is built inside the image, so nothing built outside it should ride along:
# a `dist/` from the host is a different architecture's idea of the same code.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.turbo
.docvol
.git
.github
.tanstack
**/.env
**/*.log

# The running station's own state, which is the developer's library and logs rather than anything
# the image should contain. Without these the build context is whatever music is on this machine.
**/media
**/logs
stream/music/*
!stream/music/.gitkeep

# The public website, which the image never builds and never serves. Its manifest stays, because the
# install is `--frozen-lockfile` against a lockfile that names it as a member; everything else goes,
# so that editing a page of the site does not invalidate the workspace copy and rebuild the station.
# Its dependencies are all devDependencies for the same reason: the prod prune removes them.
apps/site/*
!apps/site/package.json

# The two listener apps and the SDKs generated for them, none of which the station runs. They reached
# the image only through `COPY apps` and `COPY packages`, which made an Android-only commit rebuild
# the JavaScript workspace in all three variants and shipped the Kotlin and C# sources inside it. On a
# developer's machine the context also carried their build output, which is ignored by git and was
# not ignored here: 2.6GB of MSBuild under `apps/desktop` and 400MB of Gradle under `apps/android`,
# measured.
#
# Each app's manifest stays, for the site's reason above: it holds nothing but a name and a version
# (it exists so changesets can number the app's releases), but it makes the app a workspace member,
# and the lockfile the frozen install checks against names every member.
apps/android/*
!apps/android/package.json
apps/desktop/*
!apps/desktop/package.json
packages/sdk-kotlin
packages/sdk-csharp

# The tests, which the image has no way to run and no reason to hold. Every package keeps them in
# a top-level `tests/` beside `src/`, and every build tsconfig includes `src` alone, so this costs
# the build nothing and stops a test-only commit from invalidating the workspace copy.
**/tests

# The example plugin is built by CI and by whoever copies it, never by the image, and it sits outside
# the workspace globs. Ignored so an edit to it does not invalidate the `COPY . .` the manifests stage
# starts from.
examples/
